        {
          "id": 1710606953,
          "type": null,
          "body": "OK, I think this is fine. \n\nIEEE 802.1Q is unfortunately a bit vague about whether \"not present\" means \"the octet's value is ignored\" or \"the octet is not present at all.\" E.g., the text of Table 21-7 — Sender ID TLV format would argue for the former, but the Validation Note below it argues for the latter. I think the latter (as done here) is what is implemented, but :shrug:",
